# Pin LF in both the index and the working tree, so a checkout on Windows (where
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites files to CRLF) cannot make the same clone report
# every file as modified when it is next opened on Linux. That is exactly what
# happened here: a whole tree of phantom diffs with no content change in any of it.
#
# `text=auto` still detects binary content and leaves it untouched. The
# rules below just make that explicit for the tracked PDFs and images.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
